    "updated_at": "2026-11-08T23:00:12Z",
    "body": "I merged upstream/main into this branch; the merge applied cleanly. `scripts/gate.sh quick` on the merged branch shows the motion suites green except `swarf_pose_continuity`. That test is red on main and is fixed by #351. The worker's release `rotary_adaptive --ignored` run passed 4/4, including the previously red `adaptive_plans_the_developed_levels_under_the_load_and_kink_laws`.\n\n**For the maintainer:** this changes posted rotary-wrap (4th-axis) output only.\n- An Adaptive wrap level too narrow for the requested helix is now cut by Offset rings, with a named note.\n- A level within 1e-6 of the leave limit is now cleared over two laps.\n- Planar 2D and 3D pockets are unchanged.\n\nThe contributor's PathPilot Hub simulator (770MX) has no rotary axis, so no hands-on Hub or machine check was possible. A 4th-axis run is yours to judge. Marking ready on that basis.\n",
